      "updated": 1793889455986,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KxxOnVk7nPHeqFGMxF1wT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 402.7000126590711,
      "y": 965.2500004444446,
      "width": 71.29998779296875,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0r",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1835100111,
      "version": 49,
      "versionNonce": 1984434707,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793887290013,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "NOTES",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "NOTES",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pSuvgTMD9i8TKTL5klq9a",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 22.480285200086655,
      "y": 1002.1625112222221,
      "width": 841.0394287109375,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0s",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1842792815,
      "version": 910,
      "versionNonce": 1937028720,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793889601003,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A block lands on an SM only if there is room for it in ALL four pools at once.\n\nEach pool, alone, allows some number of blocks: \n1. thread seats / block size\n2. block seats\n3. registers / (block size x registers per thread)\n4. shared memory / shared memory per block\n\nOccupancy = warps resident / max warps the SM holds; counting threads\ngives the same ratio.\n\nRegisters per thread are set by the COMPILER, not by us. Shared memory per\nblock is set by the kernel.\n\nMy card: 1536 thread seats, 24 block seats, 65,536 registers, 100 KiB shared memory\nper SM.\n\nIf, for some reason, you ever need to do the arithmetic by hand, you need to know\nwhich card you are working with, the details of the card, and also the \nkernel's two numbers: registers per thread and shared memory per block,\nwhich come from the compiler.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A block lands on an SM only if there is room for it in ALL four pools at once.\n\nEach pool, alone, allows some number of blocks: \n1. thread seats / block size\n2. block seats\n3. registers / (block size x registers per thread)\n4. shared memory / shared memory per block\n\nOccupancy = warps resident / max warps the SM holds; counting threads\ngives the same ratio.\n\nRegisters per thread are set by the COMPILER, not by us. Shared memory per\nblock is set by the kernel.\n\nMy card: 1536 thread seats, 24 block seats, 65,536 registers, 100 KiB shared memory\nper SM.\n\nIf, for some reason, you ever need to do the arithmetic by hand, you need to know\nwhich card you are working with, the details of the card, and also the \nkernel's two numbers: registers per thread and shared memory per block,\nwhich come from the compiler.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
