      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Do you ever need to do this by hand? Rarely. The tools do it for us:\nNsight Compute reports registers per thread, achieved\noccupancy and the limiting pool per kernel, and the CUDA occupancy API on the host\nanswers \"blocks per SM for this kernel and block size\" from the compiled code.\n\nWhat the arithmetic is good for: knowing WHY a number is what it is, so when\nNsight says \"occupancy 67%, limited by registers\", you know what moved and\nwhat you can change (block size, values kept alive, register ceiling). The\ntwo choices that stay ours: the block size (a multiple of 32) and how much\nshared memory a kernel takes.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Do you ever need to do this by hand? Rarely. The tools do it for us:\nNsight Compute reports registers per thread, achieved\noccupancy and the limiting pool per kernel, and the CUDA occupancy API on the host\nanswers \"blocks per SM for this kernel and block size\" from the compiled code.\n\nWhat the arithmetic is good for: knowing WHY a number is what it is, so when\nNsight says \"occupancy 67%, limited by registers\", you know what moved and\nwhat you can change (block size, values kept alive, register ceiling). The\ntwo choices that stay ours: the block size (a multiple of 32) and how much\nshared memory a kernel takes.",
